sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor S as Staff (kiosk browser)
  box rgb(219,234,254) Purchase
    participant PURX as Purchase (not involved)
  end
  box rgb(220,252,231) Payment
    participant PAYX as Payment (not involved)
  end
  box rgb(254,243,199) Access
    participant K as Access kiosk :8003
    participant ADB as Access DB
  end
  Note over S,ADB: Grant for BK-7KQ2M9: Meeting Room A (space_id 1), code H7K3-9QXA, window [2026-10-07 09:00, 10:30).<br/>A grant also exists for Focus Pod 1 (space_id 2), BK-9MZ4RC, so Staff can select room 2
  S->>K: GET /checkin (HTTP Basic, user staff, STAFF_PASSWORD)
  K-->>S: 200 room list from space_id and space_name in stored grants, labelled "Meeting Room A (room 1)", autofocused code input (AXS-R11)
  S->>K: POST /checkin space_id=1 (no code: select Meeting Room A)
  K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, room 1 stored in the access_session cookie (AXS-R11, AXS-R18)
  Note over S,K: Each scan below is a POST with code only. The room comes from access_session.<br/>A space_id sent with a code is ignored, so a cross-site scan has no room and is refused (Select the room first).<br/>A cross-site room change (space_id, no code) is possible and accepted (ADR-0016, AXS-R11 row 10)
  Note over K: Every scan: normalise (upper-case, strip spaces and hyphens, AXS-R12),<br/>then decide in order unknown_code, revoked, wrong_room, window (AXS-R14, AXS-R13)
  alt 2026-10-07 08:50, room 1, code "h7k3 9qxa"
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=h7k3 9qxa
    K->>ADB: store scan H7K39QXA, result not_open_yet (AXS-R15)
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="not_open_yet" "opens 09:00"
  else 09:05, room 1, code H7K3-9QXA
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=H7K3-9QXA
    K->>ADB: store scan ok, grant issued to checked_in (first ok scan, AXS-R16)
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="ok" "Door unlocked (mock)"
    Note over K: The lock is mocked: ok and checked_in never prove a door opened (ADR-0017)
  else 10:10, room 1, same code again (re-entry)
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=H7K3-9QXA
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="ok" (re-entry inside the window, AXS-R13)
  else 10:30, room 1, code H7K3-9QXA
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=H7K3-9QXA
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="closed" "Check-in closed at 10:30" (end is exclusive)
  else 09:10, Staff moves the kiosk to room 2 (Focus Pod 1)
    S->>K: POST /checkin space_id=2 (no code: select Focus Pod 1)
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, room 2 stored in access_session
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=H7K3-9QXA
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="wrong_room" "This ticket is for Meeting Room A (room 1)"
  else 09:10, room 1, code of a cancelled booking (grant revoked)
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=H7K3-9QXA
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="revoked" "This ticket was cancelled"
  else 09:10, room 1, booking reference BK-7KQ2M9 typed in
    S->>K: POST /checkin code=BK-7KQ2M9
    Note over K: normalised BK7KQ2M9, no ticket code starts with BK (AXS-R06, AXS-R08)
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, data-result="unknown_code" "Code not recognised"
  else 09:10, no room in access_session (new browser, or a cross-site form)
    S->>K: POST /checkin space_id=1, code=H7K3-9QXA
    K-->>S: 303 to /checkin, flash "Select the room first", no scan stored (AXS-R11)
  end
  S->>K: GET /checkin
  K-->>S: 200 last 10 scans at room 1, newest first, masked ••••-9QXA (AXS-R15)
  Note over PURX,K: Access never calls Purchase or Payment. Purchase sent the window at issuance (AXS-R04, PUR-R27)
